        <h2>Kottu vs. Roti: What's the Difference?</h2>

        <p>Roti (godamba roti) is the base flatbread used to make kottu — a plain, slightly oily flatbread served whole, usually with a curry for dipping or wrapping. Kottu roti is what you get when that flatbread is shredded, chopped and cooked again on the griddle with other ingredients. The two dishes share the same base ingredient but are completely different eating experiences.</p>

        <p>Roti is a lighter, simpler meal — good as a snack or a quick lunch. Kottu is a full, filling, complex dish designed to satisfy after a long day. Both are excellent; both are worth eating.</p>

